{
  "description": "RFC 3339 date-time values (SPEC §4.2) as a Trust Task document's issuedAt and expiresAt carry them. Every runtime's reader must accept each `valid` value as the instant `epochMs` (milliseconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z), and refuse each `invalid` one. A value is valid when it matches YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss[.fraction](Z|±hh:mm) and every field is in range: month 1-12, a day the month has (leap years included), hour 0-23, minute and second 0-59 (no leap second), offset hours 0-23 and minutes 0-59. Each language's own date parser accepts, refuses or rolls over a different subset of the out-of-range values, so each runtime checks the ranges itself.",
